## Why This Is Asked

Tests system-level thinking for 3D reconstruction under dynamic scenes and edge-runtime constraints, plus evaluation rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Dense 3D representation (TSDF) with dynamic masking
- Lightweight pose estimation and masked fusion
- Dynamic voxel confidence and decay for occlusions
- Edge latency targets and robust evaluation metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: update TSDF with dynamic masking
function updateVoxelTSDF(voxel, depth, pose, isDynamic) {
  if (isDynamic) return; // skip static updates for dynamic voxels until confirmed
  const sdf = projectDepthToVoxel(depth, pose, voxel.coord);
  voxel.tsdf = (voxel.tsdf * voxel.weight + sdf) / (voxel.weight + 1);
  voxel.weight += 1;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you integrate semantic priors to improve dynamic masking in cluttered warehouses?
- What ablation model would you run to measure the impact of dynamic masking on map quality and drift over 5 seconds?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design cross-modal, real-time computer vision pipelines that integrate on-device adaptation with differentiable geometry for robotic manipulation and planning in unstructured environments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth and surface normals estimation from a single RGB camera
- Differentiable probabilistic mesh prediction integrated with motion planning
- Few-shot (5-shot) on-device adaptation using synthetic pre-training followed by real-world fine-tuning
- Multi-task learning with shared encoders and task-specific heads

## Code Example

```javascript
// Core inference pipeline sketch
function forwardPass(frame) {
  const features = sharedEncoder(frame);
  const depth = depthHead(features);
  const normals = normalHead(features);
  const mesh = meshHead(features);
  return { depth, normals, mesh };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify uncertainty in the mesh predictions to ensure safe manipulation?
- What strategies would you use to handle reflective or texture-less surfaces where depth estimation typically fails?
- How does the system handle dynamic scene changes between adaptation and deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end CV system design under edge constraints, occlusion and quick adaptation to new tools. It tests architectural choices, data strategy, and robust evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular pose estimation with depth priors and CAD priors
- Edge latency optimization and 40 ms budget
- 4-shot on-device adaptation; domain randomization + weak supervision

## Code Example
